2. Design Principles
Clean and professional, exam/education portal feel; content first, minimal clutter.
Consistent: every screen uses the same tokens and components. No one-off styles.
No hardcoded colors, sizes or spacing in components. Everything comes from design tokens (section 4).
Accessible: WCAG AA contrast, keyboard navigation, visible focus, ARIA labels.
Responsive: works on mobile, tablet, desktop.
Fast feeling: skeletons while loading, no layout jumping, cached data shown instantly.
Clear states: loading, empty, error, offline, slow-network, no-permission are designed for every screen.
3. Theme System [FIXED]
Two themes: Light mode and Dark mode.
User can switch from the header; the choice is saved (user preference) and applied on app start. Default follows the system preference until the user chooses.
Implemented with CSS variables (design tokens) on :root and [data-theme="dark"]. Components use tokens only, never raw color values.
Theme code lives in client/src/core/theme/ and client/src/styles/.
Theme switching must not reload the page and must not flash the wrong theme on first load.
