8. Dashboard [FIXED: widget based and customizable]
Grid of widgets the user can add, remove, move and resize; layout saved per user.
Widgets come from a widget registry (features/dashboard/widgets/). Adding a new widget means registering it, not editing the dashboard page.
Each widget has: id, title, icon, default size, min/max size, required permission, data hook, skeleton, error state, refresh.
Widget visibility depends on the user's permissions.
Dashboard works offline from cached data (read-only, layout editing disabled or saved locally per decision in PLANNING).
